{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":68727,"duration_api_ms":66918,"ttft_ms":4962,"ttft_stream_ms":1064,"time_to_request_ms":164,"num_turns":11,"result":"```json\n{\n  \"agent\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n  \"summary\": \"No infra scaffolding exists for a status endpoint today: there is no Dockerfile, no CI/CD workflow (.github/workflows is absent), and deployment is Vercel's git integration plus manual `npx vercel deploy`. Vercel already injects VERCEL_ENV and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA at build/runtime, so no new secrets are required — my work is defining the env/version contract the backend endpoint must read, documenting it in .env.example and the engineering docs, and flagging the information-disclosure and shared-resource risks. Application logic for the endpoint and the page itself belong to Backend/Frontend engineers.\",\n  \"areas_affected\": [\n    \".env.example\",\n    \"docs/engineering/PROJECT_GUIDE.md\",\n    \"docs/engineering/VERIFICATION.md\",\n    \"docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md\",\n    \"docs/ROADMAP.md (possible status note)\"\n  ],\n  \"proposed_tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Define and document the canonical source of 'version' and 'environment' values: environment = VERCEL_ENV (production/preview/development) with a NODE_ENV-based fallback for local dev where VERCEL_ENV is undefined; version = package.json `version` field, optionally combined with the short VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA when running on Vercel. Document this convention so the backend endpoint implementation has a single source of truth instead of inventing its own.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": []\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Update .env.example with a comment documenting that VERCEL_ENV / VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA are auto-injected on Vercel and absent locally, and that the status endpoint must handle that absence gracefully (no new secret env vars needed since none of this data is sensitive).\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"infra-1\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-3\",\n      \"description\": \"Document the new endpoint/page and its response contract in docs/engineering (PROJECT_GUIDE.md architecture section and/or VERIFICATION.md), and add/update the docs/index/MASTER_INDEX.md entry so `npm run docs:check` does not fail on an undiscoverable doc.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-1 (endpoint contract finalized)\"]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"infra-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Review the implemented status endpoint for information-disclosure risk before merge: confirm it returns only {status, version, environment, timestamp} and never full env var dumps, internal hostnames, or stack traces — this is a security/infra review gate, not new code.\",\n      \"suggested_owner\": \"infrastructure-engineer\",\n      \"depends_on\": [\"backend-1\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"contracts\": [\n    \"Proposed status endpoint response shape (for Backend to implement): GET /api/status -> 200 { \\\"status\\\": \\\"ok\\\" | \\\"degraded\\\" | \\\"down\\\", \\\"version\\\": string, \\\"environment\\\": \\\"production\\\" | \\\"preview\\\" | \\\"development\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": string (ISO 8601) }. No auth required if this is meant to be a public status indicator, but confirm with product (see questions).\",\n    \"Environment value must be derived from VERCEL_ENV with a local fallback (e.g. NODE_ENV === 'production' ? 'production' : 'development'), not hardcoded, so the same code works in all three Vercel environments and locally.\",\n    \"Version value must be read from package.json at build time (not hand-maintained elsewhere) to avoid drift; if commit-level granularity is wanted, append VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA.slice(0,7) when present.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"No CI/CD pipeline exists in this repo (no GitHub Actions) — `npm run verify` is run manually per AGENTS.md. The new endpoint/tests/docs will not be enforced automatically on push/PR unless the user explicitly asks for a CI workflow to be added; that is out of scope unless requested.\",\n    \"Exposing version and environment publicly is minor info disclosure — acceptable for a status page but should not be extended to leak dependency versions, internal URLs, or Supabase project refs.\",\n    \"If 'API availability' is interpreted as checking live Supabase connectivity, repeated polling by uptime monitors could add load against the single shared Supabase project (dev and prod already shared per CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md) — recommend a cheap self-check (process responding) rather than a DB round-trip, or heavy caching if DB checks are required.\",\n    \"Locally, VERCEL_ENV and VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA are undefined — without an explicit fallback the status page could render 'undefined' during local dev/testing.\"\n  ],\n  \"tests\": [\n    \"Verify the environment/version resolution logic falls back correctly when VERCEL_ENV/VERCEL_GIT_COMMIT_SHA are absent (local dev case) — unit test in Backend's test suite, but infra should confirm the fallback values match documented convention.\",\n    \"Confirm `npm run docs:check` passes after the new documentation page/section is added and indexed.\",\n    \"No new infra-owned automated tests are needed beyond the above since there is no CI pipeline to wire the endpoint into.\"\n  ],\n  \"questions_or_unknowns\": [\n    \"Should the status endpoint be publicly accessible without auth, or gated (this is a B2B marketplace, not a typical public SaaS)?\",\n    \"Does 'API availability' mean the Next.js server is responding (self-check) or that Supabase/the database is reachable? This determines whether a DB round-trip is in scope and whether infra needs to worry about load/caching.\",\n    \"Is adding a GitHub Actions CI workflow (to run `npm run verify` automatically) in scope for this feature, or does deployment remain fully manual as today?\",\n    \"Will an external uptime monitor poll this endpoint on a schedule? If so, what frequency, so caching/rate-limiting can be sized appropriately?\"\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b3aad231-3022-4464-8c39-c75ffe8d7c6e","total_cost_usd":0.40225259999999996,"usage":{"input_tokens":18279,"cache_creation_input_tokens":31887,"cache_read_input_tokens":193312,"output_tokens":6540,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":31887,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":131,"output_tokens":2242,"cache_read_input_tokens":54913,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4054},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":18279,"outputTokens":6540,"cacheReadInputTokens":193312,"cacheCreationInputTokens":31887,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.40225259999999996,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"b153fb33-338f-4671-8bb5-7f93dd1b2614"}
